#: ../../source/http-signature_http_signing.md:178
msgid "Security Considerations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-signature_http_signing.md:180
msgid "Default Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-signature_http_signing.md:182
msgid ""
"Note the default parameterization of the `Signature` scheme is only safe "
"if all requests are carried over a secure transport (i.e., TLS).  Sending"
" the default scheme over a non-secure transport will leave the request "
"vulnerable to spoofing, tampering, replay/repudiation, and integrity "
"violations (if using the STRIDE threat-modeling methodology)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-signature_http_signing.md:188
msgid "Insecure Transports"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-signature_http_signing.md:190
msgid ""
"If sending the request over plain HTTP, service providers SHOULD require "
"clients to sign ALL HTTP headers, and the `request-line`.  Additionally, "
"service providers SHOULD require `Content-MD5` calculations to be "
"performed to ensure against any tampering from clients."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-signature_http_signing.md:195
msgid "Nonces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-signature_http_signing.md:197
msgid ""
"Nonces are out of scope for this document simply because many service "
"providers fail to implement them correctly, or do not adopt security "
"specifications because of the infrastructure complexity.  Given the "
"`header` parameterization, a service provider is fully enabled to add "
"nonce semantics into this scheme by using something like an `x-request-"
"nonce` header, and ensuring it is signed with the `Date` header."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-signature_http_signing.md:204
msgid "Clock Skew"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-signature_http_signing.md:206
msgid ""
"As the default scheme is to sign the `Date` header, service providers "
"SHOULD protect against logged replay attacks by enforcing a clock skew.  "
"The server SHOULD be synchronized with NTP, and the recommendation in "
"this specification is to allow 300s of clock skew (in either direction)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-signature_http_signing.md:211
msgid "Required Headers to Sign"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-signature_http_signing.md:213
msgid ""
"It is out of scope for this document to dictate what headers a service "
"provider will want to enforce, but service providers SHOULD at minimum "
"include the `Date` header."
msgstr ""

